# bcm2837-pi3.config — BCM2837 (Raspberry Pi 3)-exclusive peripheral hardware,
# applied ONLY for --board rpi3
#
# Pi 3 is MORE architecturally different from Pi 4/Pi 5 than Pi 4 was from
# Pi 5. Three genuine hardware differences drive this fragment:
#
# 1. NO PCIe, NO xHCI USB controller, NO NVMe. hardened-k8s.config (the
#    universal base, still applied unconditionally to every board — see its
#    own header) carries CONFIG_PCIE_BRCMSTB / CONFIG_USB_XHCI_PCI /
#    CONFIG_USB_XHCI_HCD for Pi 4/5's PCIe-attached VL805/RP1 xHCI hardware.
#    BCM2837 has NONE of this silicon at all — deliberately left as harmless
#    dead Kconfig weight rather than restructured out (Option (a) — the
#    lowest-risk choice: it doesn't touch already-proven Phase 6 code and
#    matches this codebase's existing tolerance for some "compiles but never
#    binds" config elsewhere). Instead, Pi 3's USB (and its Ethernet, which is
#    USB-attached, unlike Pi 4/5's native GBit MAC) rides the SoC's
#    on-die Synopsys DesignWare USB2 OTG controller in HOST-ONLY mode:
#      - CONFIG_USB_DWC2 / CONFIG_USB_DWC2_HOST: the modern, mainline-derived
#        driver raspberrypi-sources itself defaults to for the BCM2835/2836/
#        2837 family (the RPi Foundation's older downstream tree also
#        historically shipped a "dwc_otg" driver, but dwc2 is the current
#        choice). Host-only (not dual-role/OTG gadget mode) — this board's USB
#        port is always a host in this repo's use case, same intent as Pi
#        4/5's xHCI-host-only design.
#      - CONFIG_USB_NET_SMSC95XX (+ its CONFIG_USB_USBNET/CONFIG_MII deps):
#        the ORIGINAL Raspberry Pi 3 Model B's onboard 10/100 Ethernet is not
#        a separate peripheral at all — it is one function of the SMSC (now
#        Microchip) LAN9514 USB-hub-plus-Ethernet combo chip wired to the
#        DWC2 controller above, and Linux sees it purely as a USB network
#        device (driver: smsc95xx). HIGH UNCERTAINTY (flagged explicitly):
#        this is well-documented for the specific board this phase targets
#        (BCM2837, quad-core Cortex-A53 @ 1.2GHz, 1GB RAM — the original 2016
#        Pi 3 Model B, not the 3B+ which uses a different Microchip LAN7515
#        Gigabit-capable chip) — cross-checked against Raspberry Pi hardware
#        teardowns and kernel driver-log community reports, but NOT verified
#        against a real Pi 3 boot in this sandbox (no aarch64 hardware
#        available). If real-hardware validation turns up a different chip
#        revision, only this fragment needs to change.
#
# 2. NO RP1 southbridge (Pi 5-only) and NO native BCM2711 GPIO/I2C/SPI (Pi
#    4-only) — Pi 3's GPIO-header I2C/SPI/pin-mux are the SAME long-standing
#    Broadcom bcm2835-family silicon every Pi board before Pi 5 used (Pi 1/2/
#    3/Zero/400), i.e. IDENTICAL to bcm2711-pi4.config's own hardware in this
#    respect — see that fragment's header for the parallel reasoning.
#
# 3. VideoCore IV, not VI/VII. Shares the SAME CONFIG_DRM_V3D/CONFIG_DRM_VC4
#    driver pair hardened-k8s.config already enables unconditionally for Pi
#    4/5 (the mainline vc4 KMS driver + Mesa v3d userspace driver cover the
#    whole BCM2835-through-BCM2712 VideoCore lineage) — NO extra Kconfig
#    needed here. What Pi 3 DOES need that Pi 4/5 don't is an explicit
#    dtoverlay=vc4-kms-v3d in config.txt (Pi 4/5's firmware already defaults
#    straight to KMS with no overlay at all; Pi 3's older firmware does not,
#    and falls back to a legacy non-KMS firmware-managed framebuffer this
#    repo's modern Xorg/LXDE desktop stack cannot drive) — see
#    build-rpi5-stage4.sh's VC4_OVERLAY_LINE computation and
#    specs-rpi5/boot/config.txt.tmpl. HIGH UNCERTAINTY (flagged explicitly):
#    full KMS (vc4-kms-v3d) rather than the older Fake-KMS (vc4-fkms-v3d)
#    overlay is Raspberry Pi OS's own current default for Pi 3 on a recent
#    kernel, which is why it was chosen here — but NOT verified against a
#    real Pi 3 boot in this sandbox.
#
# Applied on top of hardened-k8s.config (the universal base) for --board rpi3
# only. Format: one "scripts/config" argument set per line; lines starting
# with # are comments and are skipped.

# ── USB: Synopsys DesignWare USB2 OTG controller (host mode) ──────
enable CONFIG_USB_DWC2
enable CONFIG_USB_DWC2_HOST

# ── Ethernet: SMSC LAN9514 (USB hub + 10/100 MAC combo chip) ───────
enable CONFIG_USB_NET_SMSC95XX
enable CONFIG_USB_USBNET
enable CONFIG_MII

# ── GPIO-header I2C/SPI/pin-mux (bcm2835-family — shared with every Pi board
# before Pi 5; identical rationale to bcm2711-pi4.config) ──────────
enable CONFIG_I2C_BCM2835
enable CONFIG_SPI_BCM2835
enable CONFIG_SPI_BCM2835AUX
enable CONFIG_PINCTRL_BCM2835
